# kills: afterprint tears the print sheet down in a real browser
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern afterprint.tears tests/e2e.test.js
# teardown() closes over a getElementById() evaluated when the module runs,
# instead of re-querying inside its own body. In the unit suite's DOM stub
# every id resolves from the first line, so this looks fine. In a real browser
# #printroot (index.html:5616) has not been parsed when the app's <script>
# (index.html:3643) runs, so the reference is null and the first afterprint
# throws - the sheet is never torn down. Only the e2e run can see it.
